  <section class="chapter publications wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="publications">Selected publications</h2>
      <p>Books and papers, alongside the World Bank record of the research.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="publication-grid">
      <article class="publication publication-1" id="cybered-conflict">
        <p class="citation">Authored paper · International Conference on Cyber Conflict (CyCon) · 2016</p>
        <h3>
          <a
            class=""
            href="https://ccdcoe.org/uploads/2018/10/Art-04-Towards-a-Theory-of-Cyber-Power-the-Israeli-Experience-with-Innovation-and-Strategy.pdf"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >Towards a Theory of Cyber Power: The Israeli Experience with Innovation and Strategy&nbsp;<span
              aria-hidden="true">↗</span
            ></a
          >
        </h3>
        <p class="publication-description">
          A framework connecting strategic objectives, ways and technological means, using Israel to examine innovation
          and the economic and military dimensions of cyber power.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="publication publication-2" id="critical-infrastructure">
        <p class="citation">Coauthored paper · Journal of Cyber Policy · 2025</p>
        <h3>
          <a class="" href="https://doi.org/10.1080/23738871.2025.2451779" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >Making PROGRESS: a sectoral approach to cyber resilience and its application in sustainable
            development&nbsp;<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
          >
        </h3>
        <p class="publication-description">
          World Bank work across 11 countries in energy, healthcare, digital infrastructure and financial services. The
          institutional field record describes tailored recommendations as being implemented.
        </p>
        <a class="action" href="https://rcrl.tau.ac.il/progress_jcp_jan25" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >Institutional field record&nbsp;<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </article>
      <article class="publication publication-3" id="sectoral-cyber-resilience">
        <p class="citation">Coauthored paper · International Journal of Information Security · 2025</p>
        <h3>
          <a class="" href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s10207-024-00910-3" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >PROGRESS: the sectoral approach to cyber resilience&nbsp;<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
          >
        </h3>
        <p class="publication-description">
          A sectoral capability-maturity model connecting organizations, regulators, IT/OT supply chains and national
          cyber capabilities.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="publication publication-4" id="sectoral-maturity-model">
        <p class="citation">Supporting institutional record · World Bank · June 2023 consultation draft</p>
        <h3>
          <a
            class=""
            href="https://documents.worldbank.org/en/publication/documents-reports/documentdetail/099062623085028392"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Sectoral Cybersecurity Maturity Model&nbsp;<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
          >
        </h3>
        <p class="publication-description">
          A methodology for assessing sector cybersecurity maturity, interdependencies and critical-service resilience.
          Tabansky is credited in the cooperating Tel Aviv University research team.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
